# Shell scripts must check out with LF on every platform.
#
# Scoped to *.sh deliberately, not `* text=auto`: a blanket rule would renormalize every
# tracked file and bury real changes in a whitespace diff.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone with the default `core.autocrlf=true` writes CRLF into
# preflight.sh, agent-commit.sh and Invoke-CodexDispatch.sh. Git's own storage is already
# LF, so this is invisible in the repository and on macOS/Linux -- it only breaks in the
# adopter's working copy, where bash reads the trailing CR as part of the command and
# reports `$'\r': command not found` on the shebang line. The .sh wrapper is the canonical
# dispatch path on macOS/Linux, so that is a whole platform's entry point.
*.sh text eol=lf
